Z||000002||VISCERAL||03-09-2001||12:28 PM||||Bob Steiger's fiero depot in I believe is Loda, near you. They do conversions and everything else.<BR> <A HREF="http://twinlakesfiero.tripod.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://twinlakesfiero.tripod.com/</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Patrick Szewczyk<BR>1987 Fiero GT<BR>Silver, 5 spd, sunroof centerforce dualfriction clutch, Koni's all around, Ground Control coilovers in the rear, lowered 2" - susp.tech springs-front, poly bushings: control arms-sway bars-cradle-motor-dogbone, rear sway bar, pioneer cd player, 180 stat, 176-166 fan switch, MSD Coil, Rodney Dickman's short shifter, bushings, etc..., grand am brakes all around, k&n filter, Mustang rear scoop, next year V-8 + lowered spindles + 17x8 and 17x9" Mas Italy wheels +  235/45/17 and 255/40/17's + new paint+ custom hood vents + Mr. Mikes leather interior + 11.25" brakes w/ parking brake.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||03-09-2001||03:14 PM||||you just want to port your stock exhaust manifolds? if thats all you wanna do.. just go buy a dremel and do it yourself in 30min... a tungsten carbide bit and a little time... it's not hard... i've done 4 sets and heat tape wraped one set (killer engine bay temp reducer!)  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||MikeSchaefer||03-09-2001||03:40 PM||||Hi, how hard is it to remove the exhaust manifold?  Is this really something an ordinary joe (or mike) could do?<BR>Thanks for the response,<BR>Mike||||reg||7
Z||000005||1FST2M6||03-09-2001||04:33 PM||||got a garage, a floor jack, a 12mm, a 15mm and 17mm socket and 2" extension? i JUST yanked mine off cause the guys that hung my exhaust put too much weight on the tmanifolds and made them crack... only takes aobu 1 hour to crawl under there and yank em off... well 45min for under the car and 15 hunched over the trunk... ||||reg||1
